\section{AllGather}{
\p{An \em{AllGather} gets resources from all devices onto one device. In [TPU's](NZZ7) [[UEA0]], this is done in #{\frac{N}{2}} hops via each TPU sending its shard to the neighboring chip.}
\question{How long does it take to AllGather?}
\answer{
Assuming we have #{X} shards and the total bytes is #{N}, then each chip must send #{\frac{N}{X}} bytes. If we have an ICI bandwidth of #{W_{\text{ICI}}}, then for each chip to send to its neighbor will be
##{T_{1\text{ hop}} = \frac{N}{X\cdot W_{\text{ICI}}}}
Now each chip must send across #{X} hops, which gives #{T = X\cdot T_{1\text{ hop}} = \frac{N}{W_{\text{ICI}}}}.\sidenote{This does not change if we use the bi-directional bandwidth because then we have #{2N} bytes but only need to send at most #{\frac{X}{2}} hops!}
}
}

