\p{\strong{7:40 AM}}
\hr

\remark{
There is a \em{hop latency} incurred at each hop of approximately #{1\mu s}. This is negligible for large buffer sizes. However, for small buffers, this latency can be the bottleneck. Namely,
##{T_{1\text{ hop}} = \max\{T_{\min}, \frac{N}{W_{\text{ICI}\cdot X}}\}}
and
##{T = \max\{\frac{X\cdot T_{\min}}{2}, \frac{N}{W_{\text{ICI}}}\}}
For [ICI bandwidth of TPU v5e](676P) of #{4.5e 10}, we are latency bound when #{10^{-6} > \frac{N}{W_{\text{ICI}}} \implies N \approx 45kb}.
}

\p{\strong{8:24 AM}}
\hr
\remark{
Case 3 is effectively a distributed split-K matmul. In [tiled matmul](OGCRV), we loop over #{K} axis to perform reduction. Here, each block is computed on different device and then reduction is performed across devices\sidenote{We never want to be in case 3 for pure matmul but end up here due to model sharding strategies discussed later}.
}

